ouldn't fall flat on screen Hall of  prophecies the most intense scene in  order of the Phoenix takes place in the  Hall of prophecies a seemingly limitless  room with way too many shelves the  action was filmed on a green screen and  then the maze of shelves was added in  later but the light coming from their  wands was 100% real the cast actually  had battery packs attached to the wands  hidden underneath their clothes but  practical effects aren't always the most  comfortable Daniel Radcliffe said that  these battery packs were heavy and made  using the lumo spell a real pain walking  residential how would you feel if your  house or neighborhood ended up being  featured in a Harry Potter movie  probably pretty cool which is why the  residents of Leacock will Shire in  England were fine with the half-blood  Prince filming on their Street when  Dumbledore and Harry set off to find  Professor Slughorn they walked through  this small residential neighborhood they  filmed the scene between 5:00 p.m. and  5:00 a.m. and had to ask residents to  completely block out their windows both  so they wouldn't see the scene and also  so the set lighting wouldn't keep them  awake at night but most people probably  weren't able to sleep anyway knowing  Harry Potter was a  luring their neighborhood the cave when  Dumbledore and Harry go to the cave to  find and destroy the locket the actors  had to climb and act on realistic rock  formations some were props and some were  real but they were all placed to look  like dangerous jagged rock formations so  that the cast could convincingly  interact with their surroundings never  the conditions on which I brought you  with me this potion might paralyze me  the cave looks pretty small on set  because they digitally expanded the  scene in post-production to make it look  huge the entire background of the cave  and the creepy things living in the  water were added in later with CGI  Gringotts heist it can't be easy to do  goblet makeup on tons of different  actors but for the Gringotts heist seen  in the Deathly Hallows Part 1 the makeup  team had to get ready to make over a  whole bunch of goblins it took 8 months  of preparation to get the makeup and the  practical effects just right but the  Goblin VIP award goes to Warwick Davis  Davis spent hours and makeup every day  he was on set and the makeup artist  spent even more time making sure Davis  as many characters didn't all look  exactly the same the wand breaker  Ron Weasley isn't the only wizard with a  habit of breaking wands throughout the  entire Harry Potter series  Daniel Radcliffe was responsible for  breaking about 81 but how did he  accidentally break so many props while  he loved using the wands as drumsticks  which definitely could have been part of  it he also really liked poking his other  cast mates with them which probably  explains why so many broke in half but  considering he's the star of the  franchise we're sure the prop Department  didn't mind making him a few extras  Harry's fate most people know that Alan  Rickman was told how Snape story would  end early by JK Rowling but so was  Daniel Radcliffe Rowling told him before  the last book was published that Harry  would lose his life in one particular  scene in the final movie so Daniel  Radcliffe knew before we did that Harry  would have an epic resurrection not that  we're surprised Rowling would tell him  before us the author and the star have a  pretty good friendship that they've kept  going over the years the Room of  Requirement the Room of Requirement is  one of the most complex sets in the  Harry Potter films it became even more  complex in the Deathly Hallows part-2  when the cast had to  why mountains of furniture as the crew  literally set fire to the stage the set  was built with hundreds of actual props  fitted to scaffolding and tied to  supports so that the actors could climb  to set with harnesses the major flames  were added in later with CGI but the  crew used torches to light small fires  all over the set to make the action look  more realistic Voldemort's speech ray  Fiennes isn't just good at pulling off  Voldemort's the signature robes he also  has a way with words which is why his  speech at the end of the Deathly Hallows  part-2 was partially improvised and a  little bit different every time he gave  it the director wanted the speech to  feel authentic so he let Fiennes have  some fun with it  this was also the first time Valda Moore  was meeting Neville and it was the first  time Fiennes was acting with Matthew  Lewis even though they'd already  technically starred in five Harry Potter  films together  Rupert's strange gifts saying goodbye  isn't easy and it's even harder when  you've worked on eight films together  through your childhood but to lighten  the mood Rupert Grint decided to give  his on-screen besties some unique  presence he gave both Emma and Daniel  trumpets as parting gifts and no neither  actor played the instrument Rupert and  Emma also worked together to bring  Rupert's ice cream truck to set on the  last day of filming so that the entire  cast could have a sweet treat before  saying goodbye  which behind-the-scenes secrets  surprises you most do these onset  moments ruin the magic for you or do  they just make it that much more  impressive let us know what you think in  the comments don't forget to hit that  like button and subscribe to the things  for more thanks for watching and we'll  see you next time  you

